<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero-tag">// encrypted. viewed. destroyed.</div>
  <h1><span data-scramble>Your secrets.</span><br><span class="accent" data-scramble>Gone in one click.</span></h1>
  <p class="hero-sub">Stop pasting passwords in Slack. GhostDrop creates encrypted links that self-destruct after being read. No trace. No history. No compromise.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a href="/new" class="btn btn-lime">Create a drop</a>
    <a href="#how" class="btn btn-outline">How it works</a>
  </div>
</div>

<% if (adsenseId) { %><div class="ad-slot"><ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display:block" data-ad-client="<%= adsenseId %>" data-ad-slot="auto" data-ad-format="auto" data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins><script>(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});</script></div><% } %>

<div class="section-dark" id="how">
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-tag">// how it works</div>
    <h2>Three steps. Zero traces.</h2>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div>
        <div style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--lime);font-size:.7rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">01</div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem">Paste your secret</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.6">Password, API key, private note. Whatever you need to share. It gets AES-256-GCM encrypted before touching our database.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--lime);font-size:.7rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">02</div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem">Share the link</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.6">Get a one-time URL + QR code. Send it however you want. The actual secret never leaves our encrypted vault until the moment it's read.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--lime);font-size:.7rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">03</div>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:.4rem">It self-destructs</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--dim);font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.6">Recipient reads it. Content is permanently destroyed. You get notified. The link is dead forever. Like it never existed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="section-tag">// why this exists</div>
  <h2>Because Slack search is forever.</h2>
  <div style="max-width:700px">
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">01</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Key-separated encryption</div><div class="feat-desc">The decryption key only exists in the URL. We store a hash for lookup, not the key itself. A database breach reveals nothing.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">02</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Configurable burn</div><div class="feat-desc">One view and it's gone. Or set 5, 10, even 10,000 views for team-wide secrets. You control the blast radius.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">03</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Viewer intel</div><div class="feat-desc">Know exactly when your drop was opened, from what browser and OS. Burn notifications hit your dashboard in real-time.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">04</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Password protection</div><div class="feat-desc">Share the link in Slack. Send the password via text. Two channels, zero risk of interception on either one alone.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">05</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">Operation codenames</div><div class="feat-desc">Every drop gets a random codename like "Shadow Falcon" or "Ghost Protocol". Track drops by name, not by meaningless IDs.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div class="feat-num">06</div>
      <div><div class="feat-title">REST API</div><div class="feat-desc">Create and retrieve drops programmatically. One curl command from your CI/CD pipeline. Full docs at /api-docs.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section-dark">
  <div class="section" style="text-align:center;max-width:600px">
    <div class="section-tag">// newsletter</div>
    <h2>Security tips &amp; updates</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--dim);margin-bottom:1.5rem;font-size:.9rem">No spam. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>
    <form method="POST" action="/subscribe" style="display:flex;gap:0;border:1px solid var(--border)">
      <input type="hidden" name="source" value="landing">
      <input type="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@company.com" class="fi" style="border:none;flex:1">
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-lime" style="white-space:nowrap">Subscribe</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

